This baseline incorporates upstream contributions with their Git history:
- PR #230: public search-page transport and explicit unsupported-search errors.
- PR #231: preserve cabin class in booking deep links.
- PR #232: decode legroom independently of Wi-Fi tier.

Pre-launch work also incorporates:
- PR #160: disambiguate enum names; GLFI regenerates and tests the shipped data.
- PR #215: same-day date validation and actionable MCP validation errors.
- PR #103: adult, child, and infant controls in CLI and MCP.

GLFI additionally applies the patched curl-cffi dependency floor described in
PR #193, preserves party size in flight booking links and MCP booking tools,
and repairs same-day and filter handling in the public-page date-scan transport.

The second pre-launch batch adapts the upstream proposals:
- PR #195 (880ce1a): flexible trip-duration ranges.
- PR #196 (2779bee): independent return-time controls and builder sentinel design.
- PR #199 (23a9843): comma-separated multi-airport CLI inputs.
These PR heads were reviewed but not merged. GLFI supplies shared bounded range
execution, strict airport parsing, full-route search links, return-date pricing
integration, and nested-worker deadlock prevention for the current transport.
Selected-return fares also replace outbound starting fares in round-trip output
and cheapest-result ordering.

GLFI is not affiliated with or endorsed by Google. It uses unofficial,
reverse-engineered Google Flights endpoints, which may change or stop working.
